      "content": "Ethnic fragmentation does introduce potential risks to long-term stability in any region. While diversity can bring cultural richness, it can also create fault lines if resource distribution or political power is perceived as unfair among groups. To mitigate this, thorough due diligence on local governance structures and community relations is crucial. Understanding historical tensions and ensuring inclusive stakeholder engagement will significantly reduce the risk of internal friction affecting your investment.",
