      "content": "I hear you on the institutions part, but from a purely data-driven perspective, isn't there a noticeable correlation between these highly fragmented African demographics and higher volatility compared to, say, more homogeneous European or Asian markets? If we look at the historical data, it seems like these \"fragmented\" social structures much more frequently trend toward instability. I'm asking if, as an analyst, you'd categorize the sheer number of competing ethnic interests in a region like this as a fundamental structural weakness, regardless of how \"good\" the institutions are supposed to be.",
